    "reason": "P10-C superseded the 60 + 30 second idle policy these cases were replayed for (strict now expires an idle transaction above 120 seconds). The REST rows record only a response-to-response idle (120.345 to 121.150 seconds for commit-after-idle), so the server-side idle they observed lies within about one request round trip (1.2 to 2 seconds in recent REST recordings) of that value and its interval contains 120 seconds: no wait chosen for a replay would decide strict's answer by evidence. The P10-B and P10-C native recordings carry dispatch and response bounds for every request and decide strict's limit.",
